<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Shared SpotBugs exclusions (template-first: ships verbatim to every
  template-lineage repo; decisions and rationale recorded on
  neoforge-mod-template#52 and on the per-decision issues linked from
  agents/AGENTS.md).

  1. EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 (org-wide, #52): returning or storing a
     reference to a mutable object. In NeoForge mod code that is the idiomatic
     shape by design - fields hold Level, ItemStack, and capability objects
     because the game model IS shared mutable state; upstream SpotBugs has no
     Minecraft awareness and flags the correct pattern as a vulnerability
     (~45 findings org-wide at flip time, all noise).

  2. BC_IMPOSSIBLE_CAST inside mixin packages (#71): the cast from a mixin
     class to its target type - `(ItemStack) (Object) this` - is the canonical
     Mixin idiom for reaching the merged type, and @Shadow cannot produce a
     value of the target type. SpotBugs sees only the static types, so the
     runtime merge is invisible to it and the cast reads as impossible.

  3. MS_EXPOSE_REP on getInstance accessors (#71): exposing the one service
     instance is the singleton pattern's purpose, and every HexaHexes service
     is a stateful singleton by design (datapack reload replaces the content).
     No code shape both returns the instance and satisfies the detector;
     returning an unmodifiable copy of a stateful service would be the actual
     bug.

  4. RV_RETURN_VALUE_IGNORED_NO_SIDE_EFFECT inside wire-codec packages (#71):
     FriendlyByteBuf's fluent write methods advance the write index through
     ByteBufUtil static helpers, which the receiver-based side-effect analysis
     cannot attribute, so buffer writes read as pure. Chaining the fluent
     calls does not clear it (the tail call is still reported).

  Scope rule: these patterns only, and each entry needs an issue-first
  decision - this file must never become a dumping ground. Everything else
  (PA_PUBLIC_PRIMITIVE_ATTRIBUTE, MS_PKGPROTECT, MS_MUTABLE_COLLECTION*, and
  every correctness/security detector) stays enforced everywhere.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="BC_IMPOSSIBLE_CAST"/>
        <Class name="~org\.bitwisemadness\..*\.mixin\..*"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="MS_EXPOSE_REP"/>
        <Method name="getInstance"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="RV_RETURN_VALUE_IGNORED_NO_SIDE_EFFECT"/>
        <Class name="~org\.bitwisemadness\..*\.(network|net)\..*"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
